From 7f3e5079f7a70bc310f025c1f578a9e251dd8be2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:06:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] antinomie: checkpoint native capture and async run tracking

ANT-T0009: expand the pinned native inventory and reviewed capture families, track root-process and descendant state, and stage attributed asynchronous observations without changing V7. Preserve registered-buffer partial-read output before retry iterator advancement.

Unknown selector/context layouts and unavailable late user buffers stay explicitly incomplete; this checkpoint does not claim full semantic coverage of all 375 native slots. Verified four-vCPU lifecycle and safe exercise, byte-exact fixed read/write and partial-read retry payloads, full image build and CONFIG_ANTINOMIE=n focused objects.
